# Applies to the build context (repo root) for every Dockerfile under
# infra/docker/ -- COPY commands like `COPY apps/api .` still copy from
# the build context, so patterns here reach into subdirectories too.
# Milestone 10 finding: without this file, a real .env dropped into
# apps/api/ or apps/web/ (a natural, gitignored, commonly-used location
# with pydantic-settings' env_file=".env") would be baked directly into
# the image layers. Never allow that regardless of what ends up on disk
# in a checkout -- .env.example is intentionally NOT excluded here since
# it holds placeholders only and is safe (and useful) to ship.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

.git
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
